From 467bcac5198df17371aec6c954c88ede77ebf774 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "MOTOR-46 (Claude)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:49:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] sync: account crypto for the FlyWeb 3.2 sync account (H3)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

FlyWeb/docs/sync-cuenta.md §3.1, §4 and §11; protocol of the server in
FlyWeb/servidor/sync/cuenta/README.md (softmac PR #977).

New components/brave_sync/crypto/account_crypto.{h,cc}, all BoringSSL from
the tree, nothing macOS-specific and nothing new in third_party:

- email and password normalisation (trim, simple lower case, NFC; the
  password only NFC), as the server does it;
- KE = scrypt(password, SHA-256("flyweb-cuenta-v1" || email), 2^17, 8, 1)
  with max_mem 130 MiB (the default 65 MiB fails), and KL/KU split from KE
  with HKDF-SHA256;
- the seed wrap E = nonce || AES-256-GCM(KU, seed, ad = "flyweb-envoltura-v1"
  || SHA-256(email)) and its open, which refuses any changed wrap (P15);
- the chain keys derived from the seed exactly like
  BraveSyncAuthManager::DeriveSigningKeys (not touched), and the one-use
  chain proof: Ed25519 over "flyweb-cuenta-v1" || lp(method) || lp(path) ||
  lp(op) || lp(account) || lp(nonce) || SHA-256(body).

KE, KL, KU and seeds live in SecretKey, wiped with OPENSSL_cleanse; ASCII
passwords never go through ICU.

Known-answer tests computed outside Chromium (Python), including the go-sync
client_id of brave_sync_auth_manager_unittest.cc for the same words and the
real-cost scrypt (logs the time: input for P23).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
